.\" oh-my-dock CLI manual — source: CLI/ohmydock.1 (shipped in OhMyDock.app/Contents/Resources/)
.Dd October 20, 2026
.Dt OHMYDOCK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ohmydock
.Nd control oh-my-dock profiles and the macOS Dock from the command line
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -quiet
.Op Fl -no-color
.Op Fl -yes
.Op Fl -non-interactive
.Op Fl -lock-timeout Ar seconds
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Pp
.Nm
.Op Fl -version
.Pp
.Nm
.Op Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility drives oh-my-dock headlessly.
It links the same
.Lk Packages/OhMyDockCore OhMyDockCore
library as the menu-bar app.
The app does not need to be running.
.Pp
When
.Fl -json
is set, stdout is exactly one JSON document (envelope
.Va schemaVersion
1).
The process exit code is the contract; human-readable text is not stable.
.Pp
Shell completion scripts are available via
.Cm completions
(see
.Sx EXAMPLES ) .
.Pp
Never pass
.Fl -allow-quit
unless the user agreed to quit the apps listed in a dry-run or JSON
.Va willQuit
payload.
.Fl -yes
alone does not authorize quits.
Do not edit
.Pa ~/Library/Preferences/com.apple.dock.plist
directly or run
.Cm killall Dock .
URL scheme
.Lk ohmydock://
links are handled by the menu-bar app, not this CLI.
.Ss Environment
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev OHMYDOCK_SUPPORT_DIR
Absolute path to the support directory (default
.Pa ~/Library/Application Support/oh-my-dock/ ) .
Relative paths are rejected (exit 2).
.It Ev OHMYDOCK_LOCK_TIMEOUT
Lock timeout in seconds (same as
.Fl -lock-timeout ) .
.It Ev NO_COLOR
When set, disables color on human output.
.El
.Ss Files
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/Library/Application Support/oh-my-dock/
Profiles, snapshots, and lock files
.Pq Pa operation.lock ,
.Pa preview.lock ) .
.It Pa OhMyDock.app/Contents/Helpers/ohmydock
CLI binary inside the app bundle (Homebrew cask symlinks this path).
.It Pa OhMyDock.app/Contents/Helpers/dockutil
Bundled dockutil helper used for Dock mutations.
.El
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global flags may appear before or after the subcommand.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -json
Emit one JSON document on stdout for success or failure.
.It Fl -quiet
Minimal stdout on success (see design: list still prints names when quiet).
.It Fl -no-color
Disable ANSI color on human output.
.It Fl -no-color
Also disabled when the
.Ev NO_COLOR
environment variable is set or stdout is not a TTY.
.It Fl -yes
Assume defaults; never prompt.
Required together with
.Fl -allow-quit
when
.Cm apply
would quit apps.
.It Fl -non-interactive
Non-interactive mode (v0.3 never prompts; reserved for later).
.It Fl -lock-timeout Ar seconds
Lock acquire timeout in seconds;
.Ar 0
means try once.
Default 180 unless overridden by
.Ev OHMYDOCK_LOCK_TIMEOUT .
.It Fl -version
Print version and exit (same as
.Cm version ) .
.It Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Pp
.Fl -allow-quit ,
.Fl -dry-run ,
.Fl -quit-scope ,
and
.Fl -keep-running
are valid only on
.Cm apply ;
elsewhere they are usage errors (exit 2).
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm list
List saved Dock profiles.
.It Cm show Ar profile
Show a profile document.
.Ar profile
is a name or UUID.
.It Cm current
Compare the live Dock to saved profiles.
.It Cm apply Ar profile
Apply a profile to the Dock.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -dry-run
Preview without writing (exit 0 when preview computed).
.It Fl -allow-quit
Allow quitting apps (requires
.Fl -yes ) .
.It Fl -quit-scope Ar previous | all | none
Override quit scope for this apply only.
.It Fl -keep-running Ar bundleId
Keep the given bundle ID running (repeatable).
.El
.It Cm save Ar name
Save the current Dock as a profile.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -force
Replace tiles of an existing profile with the same name.
.It Fl -include-prefs
Capture Dock preference keys onto the profile.
.El
.It Cm delete Ar profile
Delete a saved profile (requires
.Fl -yes ) .
.It Cm rename Ar profile Ar new-name
Rename a profile.
.It Cm duplicate Ar profile Ar new-name
Duplicate a profile under a new name.
.It Cm undo
Restore the previous Dock snapshot.
.It Cm snapshots
List snapshots (default subcommand).
.It Cm history
Alias for
.Cm snapshots list .
.It Cm snapshots Cm pin Ar id
Pin a snapshot by UUID.
.It Cm snapshots Cm unpin Ar id
Unpin a snapshot.
.It Cm snapshots Cm delete Ar id
Delete a snapshot (requires
.Fl -yes ) .
.It Cm snapshots Cm restore Ar id
Restore a snapshot (requires
.Fl -yes ) .
.It Cm restore Ar id
Restore a snapshot (requires
.Fl -yes ) .
.It Cm export Ar profile
Export a profile.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -format Ar json | script
Output format (default
.Cm json ) .
.It Fl -output Ar file
Write to a file instead of stdout.
.It Fl -force
Overwrite an existing output file.
.El
.It Cm import Ar file
Import a profile file, or a single hyphen for stdin (must be piped, not a TTY).
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -name Ar name
Use this name when the sanitized name is taken.
.El
.It Cm status
Report app, lock, and active profile status.
.It Cm doctor
Run environment checks (exit 0 when no check failed).
.It Cm version
Print oh-my-dock version.
.It Cm completions Ar zsh | bash | fish
Print a shell completion script.
Does not support
.Fl -json
(exit 2).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success, including idempotent
.Cm apply
with
.Va noChanges .
.It 1
Internal error
.Pq Va error.code No internal .
.It 2
Usage error
.Pq Va error.code No usage ,
bad arguments, unknown command,
.Fl -allow-quit
off
.Cm apply ,
TTY stdin import,
relative
.Ev OHMYDOCK_SUPPORT_DIR ,
.Cm completions
with
.Fl -json .
.It 3
Not found
.Pq Va error.code No notFound ;
undo with nothing to undo uses
.Va nothingToUndo .
.It 4
Ambiguous profile name
.Pq Va error.code No ambiguous .
.It 5
Needs confirmation
.Pq Va error.code No needsConfirmation :
apply would quit or skip apps without required flags.
Nothing is written.
.It 6
Conflict
.Pq Va error.code No conflict :
name in use, export refused, invalid profile, etc.
.It 7
Busy
.Pq Va error.code No locked :
operation or preview lock held.
.It 8
Apply failed and rolled back
.Pq Va rolledBack
or rollback failed
.Pq Va rollbackFailed .
.It 130
Interrupted
.Pq Dv SIGINT ;
apply may roll back first.
.El
.Pp
Validation errors from ArgumentParser map to exit 2, not 64.
.Sh EXAMPLES
List profiles as JSON:
.Pp
.Dl ohmydock --json list
.Pp
Dry-run an apply before switching:
.Pp
.Dl ohmydock apply Work --dry-run --json
.Pp
Apply without quitting apps:
.Pp
.Dl ohmydock apply Work --quit-scope none --yes
.Pp
Install zsh completions:
.Pp
.Dl eval "$(ohmydock completions zsh)"
.Pp
.Dl eval "$(ohmydock completions bash)"
.Pp
.Dl ohmydock completions fish | source
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Lk https://github.com/Farzin-Firoozi/oh-my-dock oh-my-dock on GitHub
